# Haran AI (حرّان) — Master System Rules (v2: English pivot)

## Identity & Role
You are an expert full-stack AI engineer developing "Haran AI": an autonomous
agro-pastoral monitoring system for Tunisian family farms (olive groves +
cattle). This is a hackathon prototype. All UI text, spoken output, and
model-generated diagnosis text are in ENGLISH for this build. Tunisian Derja
voice is the stated production target but is explicitly out of scope right
now (browser TTS has no reliable Tunisian Derja voice, ar-TN routinely fails
or falls back silently) — do not generate Arabic-script text or ar-TN/ar lang
codes anywhere in this codebase unless explicitly asked again later.

## Target Audience & UX Constraints
- Users range from 20 to 80 years old, many with limited literacy — this is
  still true even in English. Keep it voice-first and zero-typing.
- ZERO-TYPING UI: massive touch targets, high-contrast dark palette
  (slate-900 background #0f172a, emerald green #10b981, alert red #ef4444).
- VOICE-FIRST: diagnoses and alerts speak aloud via browser native
  `window.speechSynthesis`, lang code `en-US`. Never introduce paid
  third-party voice APIs.

## Tech Stack & Port Mappings
- Unified Backend: Python 3.10+, FastAPI, Uvicorn, OpenCV, Ultralytics
  YOLOv8n, python-dotenv. Runs on port 8000.
- Frontend: React + Vite, Leaflet + React-Leaflet (ESRI World Satellite
  Imagery tiles), Lucide-React icons. Runs on port 5173.
- Multimodal Vision: Groq Cloud API, model
  `meta-llama/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct` (the previously used
  `llama-3.2-11b-vision-preview` was decommissioned by Groq in April 2025 and
  will always error — never use it again).
- Cow CCTV Stream: Local OpenCV + YOLOv8n streaming MJPEG over HTTP
  (`/api/cow-stream`).

## Mandatory Code Standards
1. NO PLACEHOLDERS: generate complete, production-ready files, no `// TODO`
   or truncated sections.
2. ENVIRONMENT SECRETS: load via `python-dotenv` from `backend/.env`. Always
   keep `backend/.env.example` current and `.gitignore` excluding `.env`,
   `venv/`, `node_modules/`, and heavy weights (`*.pt`).
3. OFFLINE DEMO RESILIENCE: every Groq call must have an immediate fallback
   mock diagnosis (English) so the demo never fails on weak hackathon Wi-Fi.
   Log clearly to the terminal whether a response came from the real model
   or the fallback, so we can tell during testing which path fired.
4. SINGLE UNIFIED BACKEND: leaf diagnosis and cow video stream both run
   inside the one Python FastAPI backend. Do not add a separate Node backend.
5. CORS: full CORS (`*`) on FastAPI for `http://localhost:5173`.
6. LANGUAGE: all model prompts, UI strings, and TTS output are English only
   in this build. Do not emit Arabic-script text, ar-TN, or ar lang codes.
